/target
# Bench output stays ignored (reports, criterion dirs), but the committed
# ADR-0070 tier B baseline under bench/baselines/ is tracked. Re-including a
# path requires not excluding its parent directory itself, so exclude the
# contents of bench/ (bench/*) rather than the directory, then re-include the
# baselines subtree. See issue #533.
/bench/*
!/bench/baselines/
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
.DS_Store
/rustfs-data
/examples/otlp_metrics_fixture.pb
__pycache__/
/.superpowers/
/.cache/
node_modules/

# Per-developer Claude Code config and its helper scripts. .claude/settings.json
# is the team's; anything machine-specific belongs in these instead.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/helpers/

# graft's local graph cache - regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
graft/

# Local, per-checkout state for .claude/guards/epic-status-nudge.mjs.
.claude/.epic-status-nudge-state.json

# scripts/epic-orchestrator.sh's per-epic index. The epic issue body is the
# durable ledger; this is a local cache of it plus the CI signatures seen on
# a head, so it is per-machine and never committed.
.claude/epic-state/

# The disk watchdog drops this in the scope directory when it fires; the
# harness commit-on-death sweeps an unignored file into a wip commit.
.disk-watchdog-fired
# Fleet executors write gate logs and any cargo-install tree inside the
# checkout, because $HOME on the amd64 executor class is a 1 GB tmpfs and
# /tmp is the harness capture filesystem. Ignored for the same reason as
# the watchdog marker above: commit-on-death must not sweep them in.
.gate-logs/
.dd-tools/
